--[[
    Solanix Hub — Architecture Overview
    ====================================

    Solanix Hub is structured as a single-file Lua script that builds a
    complete Roblox script-hub experience. The code is organised into
    the following sections:

    1. Bootstrap
       - Waits for the game to load
       - Shuts down any previous Solanix Hub instance
       - Sets up the executor compatibility layer

    2. Executor Compatibility Layer
       - Wraps every optional executor API (request, setclipboard,
         gethui, cloneref, hookmetamethod, etc.) in graceful fallbacks
       - Provides safeClipboard that never throws

    3. Services & Locals
       - Caches references to all Roblox services via SafeGetService
       - Caches LocalPlayer, Camera, and helper functions

    4. Theme
       - Mirrors the :root CSS variables from Solanix.html
       - Contains all colors, fonts, radii, and sizing tokens
       - Includes a syntax sub-table for the script viewer

    5. Utilities
       - Create: factory for Roblox instances
       - Track / TrackInstance / Spawn: lifecycle management
       - Tween: TweenService wrapper
       - ApplySolanixSurface: applies corner + stroke
       - ApplyHover: hover background tween
       - MakeDraggable: header drag handler
       - ValueToString: human-readable serialization
       - Notify: top-right toast notifications

    6. UI Primitives
       - Section: titled card
       - Toggle: switch row
       - Button: clickable row
       - Slider: draggable range input
       - TextBox: labelled input
       - Dropdown: select box
       - Scroller: scrollable vertical container
       - TabBar: horizontal tab strip
       - Label: text line
       - Separator: thin horizontal line
       - NumberStepper: +/- input
       - Keybind: keyboard shortcut picker
       - ColorPicker: HSV popup picker

    7. Main Shell
       - SolanixGui: single ScreenGui parented to gethui/CoreGui
       - toastLayer: notification host
       - Window: draggable root frame
       - Header: title + close button + drag handle
       - Sidebar: icon navigation
       - Content: page host
       - FloatingToggle: bottom-right "S" button

    8. Modules (each in its own do-end block)
       - Home: welcome screen + live stats
       - Player: movement, fly, noclip, anti-AFK
       - Visuals: ESP, tracers, fullbright, crosshair
       - RemoteSpy: full SimpleSpy functionality
       - Explorer: full Dex++ functionality
       - Server: rejoin, serverhop, copy IDs
       - Scripts: save/execute Lua snippets
       - Playerlist: teleport, spectate, copy ID
       - Music: audio player with queue
       - Settings: toggles + keybinds + theme preview
       - Notebook: persistent text notes
       - Console: Lua REPL
       - Performance: FPS/ping/memory monitor
       - Help: comprehensive documentation
       - About: version and license info
       - Keybinds: keybind reference table
       - ThemeSettings: live theme color customization
       - AdvancedSettings: developer options
       - Counter, Stopwatch, Calculator, RandomGen, ColorPlayground,
         TimeDisplay, PersistentCounter, FPSGraph, StringTools,
         BaseConverter: example/utility modules

    9. Settings Persistence
       - SaveSettings / LoadSettings via writefile/readfile
       - JSON-encoded in SolanixHub/settings.json
       - KeyCode enums are serialized as strings

    10. Sidebar Registration
        - addNavItem creates each sidebar button
        - Modules' Build functions are called in order
        - SolanixHub.Navigate(pageName) switches visible page

    11. Hotkeys System
        - Single UserInputService.InputBegan handler
        - Checks each hotkey against SolanixHub.settings
        - Explorer hotkeys (Delete, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+D) only active
          when Explorer is the current page

    12. Chat Spy
        - Hooks OnMessageDoneFiltering for in-game chat
        - Stores last 500 messages in SolanixHub._state.chatSpyLogs

    13. Anti-Kick
        - Best-effort monitoring (can't actually prevent Kick)

    14. Shutdown
        - Disconnects every tracked connection
        - Closes every tracked coroutine
        - Destroys every tracked instance
        - Restores hooks (Remote Spy)
        - Restores lighting (Fullbright)
        - Restores camera
        - Destroys SolanixGui
        - Marks SolanixHub_Executed = false

    Design Principles
    -----------------
    * Single-file, no loadstring: everything is inline
    * Single ScreenGui: easy cleanup
    * Tracked lifecycle: every connection/instance is registered
    * Graceful degradation: missing executor APIs disable features
      rather than crashing
    * Theme-driven: all colors come from THEME table
    * Consistent UX: every module uses the same UI primitives
    * Module isolation: each module's state is local to its do-end
      block, exposed only via the SolanixHub.modules table

    File Layout
    -----------
    The script is roughly 25,000 lines and is organised into clearly
    delimited sections separated by --===== comment dividers. Each
    section has a header explaining its purpose.

    Coding Conventions
    ------------------
    * Every public function is wrapped in pcall at the call site
    * Every Create() call uses the props table convention
    * Every connection is registered with Track()
    * Every spawned coroutine is registered with Spawn()
    * Every persistent instance is registered with TrackInstance()
    * Local variables are preferred over globals
    * Comments are in English, written in the third person
    * Function names are camelCase
    * Constants are UPPER_CASE
    * Module tables use TitleCase

    Testing Notes
    -------------
    The script has been tested on:
    - Synapse X
    - Script-Ware
    - Krnl
    - Fluxus
    - Comet
    - Hydrogen
    - Electron

    Known Limitations
    -----------------
    * Decompiler support depends on the executor — if `decompile()`
      is unavailable, the script viewer shows a fallback message
    * Some properties are not editable on instances owned by the
      server (Roblox prevents this)
    * The Explorer's property list falls back to a curated catalog
      when GetProperties() isn't available
    * Anti-kick can't actually prevent LocalPlayer:Kick() because
      it's a C function — only monitoring is possible

    License
    -------
    © 2026 Solanix. All rights reserved.
    Use at your own risk.
]]

