    remoteSpyGuide = [[
REMOTE SPY GUIDE
================

The Remote Spy module intercepts every FireServer and InvokeServer
call made by the game (and optionally by you). Each call is logged
with its arguments serialized as Lua code, ready to copy and paste
into your own scripts.

Basic Usage
-----------
1. Navigate to the Remote Spy page (sidebar or F2).
2. Click the "Spy: OFF" button in the top-right to enable capture.
   It should turn green and say "Spy: ON".
3. Interact with the game — every remote call will appear in the
   left panel, grouped by remote name.
4. Click any call to see its generated code in the top-right panel.
5. Use the "Copy" button or Ctrl+C to copy the code to your clipboard.

Filters
-------
- ALL: show all remotes
- RE:  show only RemoteEvents
- RF:  show only RemoteFunctions
- Search box: filter by remote name (case-insensitive)

Actions
-------
- Run Selected Calls: re-fires the selected remote(s) with the
  captured arguments.
- Spam Selected: continuously fires the selected remote(s) at 10Hz.
- Block Selected (i): blocks this specific remote instance from
  reaching the server (still logged).
- Block Selected (n): blocks all remotes with this name.
- Exclude Selected (i): stops logging this specific remote instance.
- Exclude Selected (n): stops logging all remotes with this name.
- Decompile Calling Script: attempts to decompile the script that
  fired the remote (requires decompile() in your executor).

Multiselect
-----------
- Ctrl+Click: toggle individual selection
- Shift+Click: range select from last clicked to current

Hotkeys
-------
- F2: toggle the Remote Spy GUI
- F3: toggle spy capture on/off
- F4: clear all logs
- F5: toggle spam of selected remotes

Limitations
-----------
- Without hookmetamethod/hookfunction, the spy cannot intercept calls
  and will show an error notification.
- Some remotes fire very frequently (e.g. heartbeat remotes). Use
  Exclude to filter them out.
- The decompiler requires executor support. If unavailable, the script
  viewer shows a fallback message.
]],

