    faq = [[
FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS
==========================

Q: Why doesn't the spy capture anything?
A: Make sure spy is toggled ON (the button in the top-right turns
   green). If it stays red, your executor doesn't support
   hookmetamethod or hookfunction, which are required to intercept
   remote calls.

Q: Why does the Explorer show only some properties?
A: Roblox doesn't expose a public GetProperties() API on older
   clients. We fall back to a curated list of common properties
   for each class type.

Q: Can I save my settings across sessions?
A: Yes — settings are saved to SolanixHub/settings.json via
   writefile(). Make sure your executor supports the file API.

Q: Does this work on mobile executors?
A: Mostly. Touch dragging works on the header, but some hotkeys
   require a physical keyboard.

Q: How do I add my own snippets to the Scripts module?
A: Open SolanixHub/scripts.json in your executor's file browser and
   add entries to the array. Each entry should be {"name": "...",
   "code": "..."}.

Q: Can I use the Remote Spy to spam remotes?
A: Yes — select one or more calls, then click "Spam Selected" or
   press F5. The script will re-fire each call 10 times per second.

Q: Does ESP work through walls?
A: Yes — the Highlight instances use DepthMode = AlwaysOnTop, so
   they're visible regardless of geometry.

Q: Why does my game crash when I enable Noclip?
A: Some anti-cheats detect CanCollide changes. If that happens,
   disable Noclip and use Fly instead (which doesn't modify
   collision).

Q: How do I report a bug?
A: Solanix Hub is provided as-is without warranty. If you find a
   bug, you can fix it yourself — the entire source is in this
   single file.

Q: Is this script safe?
A: The script doesn't make any external HTTP requests (except for
   the optional Server Hop API). It doesn't exfiltrate data. Use
   at your own risk, as with any executor script.
]],
}

