-- COMPREHENSIVE FINAL SHUTDOWN NOTES
--=====================================================================

--[[
    Shutdown Procedure
    ==================

    When SolanixHub_Shutdown() is called (or the close button is clicked),
    the following cleanup steps occur:

    1. Disconnect every tracked connection (SolanixHub._connections)
       Each connection is wrapped in pcall to ensure one failure
       doesn't prevent the rest from being disconnected.

    2. Close every tracked coroutine (SolanixHub._threads)
       Uses coroutine.close() which is available in Luau.

    3. Destroy every tracked instance (SolanixHub._instances)
       Includes the main ScreenGui, which cascades destruction to all
       child UI elements.

    4. Restore hooks (Remote Spy)
       If the spy was active, the original __namecall, FireServer,
       and InvokeServer functions are restored via hookfunction.

    5. Restore lighting (if Fullbright was on)
       Lighting.Brightness, ClockTime, FogEnd, GlobalShadows, Ambient
       are restored to their pre-Fullbright values.

    6. Restore camera
       Camera.CameraType is set back to Custom, and CameraSubject is
       set back to the LocalPlayer's humanoid.

    7. Destroy the main ScreenGui
       This is the final cleanup step. After this, no Solanix Hub UI
       exists in the game.

    8. Mark as not-executed
       getgenv().SolanixHub_Executed = false, so a re-run of the
       script will work cleanly.

    9. Clear getgenv().SolanixHub_Shutdown
       So the next run can set a fresh shutdown function.

    Memory Leaks
    ------------
    All connections, instances, and threads are tracked in centralized
    tables. This ensures that shutdown can clean up everything in one
    pass. If a module creates something without using Track / TrackInstance
    / Spawn, it will leak. Module authors must use these helpers.

    Re-entrancy
    -----------
    The shutdown function is idempotent — calling it twice is safe.
    The second call will simply iterate over empty tables and do nothing.

    Error Handling
    --------------
    Every cleanup step is wrapped in pcall. If one step fails (e.g.
    an instance is already destroyed), the others still run. The
    shutdown function never throws.
]]

