    8. Module System
    ----------------
    Each module is a table in SolanixHub.modules with a Build function:

        SolanixHub.modules.MyModule = {}
        function SolanixHub.modules.MyModule.Build()
            local page = SolanixHub.NewPage("MyModule")
            -- build UI here
        end

    Modules are registered in the sidebar via addNavItem(order, name,
    glyph, label) and built in order. After all modules build, the
    Home page is shown.

    Each module can expose additional API:

        function SolanixHub.modules.MyModule.DoThing()
            ...
        end

    Other modules can call SolanixHub.modules.MyModule.DoThing().

    9. Remote Spy Internals
    -----------------------
    The Remote Spy hooks:
    - __namecall via hookmetamethod
    - FireServer via hookfunction on a probe RemoteEvent
    - InvokeServer via hookfunction on a probe RemoteFunction
    - UnreliableRemoteEvent.FireServer similarly

    For each intercepted call:
    - Check if it's a Remote (IsA check)
    - Skip if checkcaller() returns true (don't log our own calls)
    - Get DebugId for blacklist/blocklist lookup
    - Deep-clone the args (handles Instance references via cloneref)
    - Add to the log with generated Lua code

    Block list: prevents the call from reaching the server.
    Exclude list: skips logging entirely.

    Code generation produces:
        local remote = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage").RemoteEvent
        remote:FireServer(arg1, arg2, ...)

    Multiselect:
    - Ctrl+Click: toggle individual log
    - Shift+Click: range select

    Spam:
    - Re-fires selected remotes every 0.1 seconds
    - Uses task.spawn so it doesn't block UI

    10. Explorer Internals
    ----------------------
    The Explorer builds a lazy-loaded recursive tree:
    - Each row has an arrow to expand/collapse
    - Children are loaded only when first expanded
    - Children are sorted alphabetically by name

    Properties panel:
    - Uses SolanixHub._fullClassCatalog as a fallback property list
    - Each property is rendered by SolanixHub.PropertyEditors.Dispatch
      which picks the right editor based on typeof()

    Selection history:
    - Every selection is pushed to a history stack
    - Back/Forward buttons navigate the stack

    Context menu (right-click):
    - Copy Path, Copy Name, Copy ClassName
    - Spy this Remote (jumps to Remote Spy)
    - Decompile Script
    - Clone, Destroy

    Hotkeys (Explorer only):
    - Delete: destroy selected
    - Ctrl+C: copy path
    - Ctrl+D: clone

    11. Settings Persistence
    ------------------------
    Settings are stored in SolanixHub/settings.json via writefile.
    On load, LoadSettings() reads the file and merges with defaults.
    On change, SaveSettings() writes the file.

    KeyCode enums are serialized as strings ("RightShift", "F3", etc.)
    and deserialized back to Enum.KeyCode on load.

    If writefile is unavailable, settings are kept in-memory only.

    12. Hotkeys System
    ------------------
    A single UserInputService.InputBegan handler checks each hotkey:

        Track(UserInputService.InputBegan:Connect(function(inp, gp)
            if gp then return end
            if inp.UserInputType ~= Enum.UserInputType.Keyboard then return end
            local kc = inp.KeyCode
            local s = SolanixHub.settings
            if kc == (s.hotkey_toggleWindow or Enum.KeyCode.RightShift) then
                Window.Visible = not Window.Visible
            elseif kc == (s.hotkey_toggleSpy or Enum.KeyCode.F3) then
                SolanixHub.modules.RemoteSpy.ToggleSpy()
            ...
            end
        end))

    Explorer hotkeys are only active when currentPage == "Explorer".

    13. Shutdown Procedure
    ----------------------
    SolanixHub_Shutdown():
    1. Disconnect every tracked connection
    2. Close every tracked coroutine
    3. Destroy every tracked instance
    4. Restore hooks (Remote Spy)
    5. Restore lighting (Fullbright)
    6. Restore camera
    7. Destroy SolanixGui
    8. Set SolanixHub_Executed = false
    9. Clear SolanixHub_Shutdown

    Every step is wrapped in pcall. The function is idempotent.

    14. API Reference
    -----------------
    See the inline API reference section above for the full list of
    exposed functions and tables.

    15. Best Practices
    ------------------
    When extending Solanix Hub with your own modules:

    - Always use Track() for connections
    - Always use TrackInstance() for persistent instances
    - Always use Spawn() for coroutines
    - Wrap risky operations in pcall
    - Use THEME colors, not hardcoded values
    - Use SolanixHub.NewPage(name) to create your page
    - Use SolanixHub.Notify() for user feedback
    - Use SolanixHub._tableUtils / _stringUtils / etc. for common ops
    - Don't create globals — keep everything in SolanixHub.*
    - Document your module's purpose and API in a comment block

    16. Troubleshooting
    -------------------
    Q: The script doesn't show up
    A: Check that your executor supports the basic APIs (gethui,
       CoreGui, etc.). Try running `print("hello")` first.

    Q: The Remote Spy shows nothing
    A: Your executor needs hookmetamethod or hookfunction. Toggle the
       spy ON (green button). Trigger some in-game actions.

    Q: The Explorer doesn't show all properties
    A: Roblox doesn't expose GetProperties() on the client. We fall
       back to a curated catalog. For comprehensive coverage, use a
       server-side explorer.

    Q: Settings don't persist
    A: Make sure writefile and readfile are available. Check that
       the SolanixHub/ folder was created.

    Q: Some modules fail to build
    A: Check the console (F9 in Roblox) for warning messages. Each
       failed module is logged with its error.

    17. Limitations
    ---------------
    - Decompiler requires executor support (decompile() function)
    - Anti-kick can't actually prevent LocalPlayer:Kick() (C function)
    - Some properties are read-only on the client (server-owned)
    - GetProperties() isn't available on older Roblox clients
    - Nil instances require getnilinstances() support
    - Mobile executors may lack keyboard support for hotkeys

